      "writtenOn": "2019-12-19T19:05:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like some also use StaticServiceFetcher. Per their class comments:\n\nCachedServiceFetcher is used when the system service constructor needs a ContextImpl and should be cached by that context.\n\nStaticServiceFetcher is used when the system does not need a ContextImpl and should be cached process-wide.\n\nStaticApplicationContextServiceFetcher has a TODO on it stating that it should be removed when ConnectivityManager works well when several application components have their own instances. Based on this, I think we should avoid adding more dependencies on it.\n\n\nFor now, replacing with CachedServiceFetcher.",
